/*!
\page page_gettingstarted Getting started

The program can be started from the command line. General form of command line parameters is:
\verbatim
alamDMC  module_name  configuration_file
\endverbatim

The `alamDMC` provides the following modules:

-# `ASR`: Arbitrary Stress Response
-# `TSA`  Tensile Stress Analysis
-# `Q`    calculation of q-values, r-values and s-values 
-# `Yld`  calculation of yield locus section.

Each of the modules has its own configuration file format. Fortunately, there are substantial similarities between the configurations files. See \ref page_configuration for detailed description of the configuration files.

*/
